      "metadata": {
        "async": false,
        "generativeJourney": {
          "enableZeroTurnMode": false,
          "exitConditions": [
            {
              "name": "account",
              "prompt": "The caller has confirmed they need help with account balances, account details, or account activity."
            },
            {
              "name": "card",
              "prompt": "Caller confirmed card support: lost/stolen card, blocked card, declined card purchase, unrecognized card charge, damaged card, replacement, or another card issue."
            },
            {
              "name": "transfer",
              "prompt": "The caller has confirmed they need help sending money or resolving a bank transfer problem."
            },
            {
              "name": "Vip",
              "prompt": "the user has a vip credential."
            }
          ],
          "maxSteps": 10,
          "maxTokens": 8192,
          "modelType": "anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5",
          "prompt": "You are River, AnyBank's telephone assistant.\n\nYour task is to understand why the caller is contacting the bank.\nAsk: \"How can I help you today?\"\n\nIdentify whether the request concerns:\n- Accounts: balances, account details, or account activity.\n- Cards: lost/stolen cards, blocked cards, declined card purchases, unrecognized card charges, damaged cards, replacements, or other card issues. Bank transfers belong to transfers.\n- Transfers: sending money or problems with a transfer.\n-Vip: is a vip member that need any request.\n\nIf the request is unclear, ask one short clarifying question.\nIf it is outside these categories, do not force a classification.\n\nOnce you understand the request, briefly confirm it with the caller.\n\nSpeak naturally, using short sentences suitable for a phone call.\nAsk one question at a time.\nDo not request account numbers, card numbers, passwords, or PINs.\nDo not claim to check banking data or transfer the call.\nAfter identifying the request, ask the caller to confirm your understanding.\nIf they correct you, clarify their request before proceeding.\nOnce they confirm, exit through the matching condition.",
          "promptVersion": "latest",
          "temperature": 0.2,
          "tools": []
        },
        "name": "",
        "stateModifications": []
      },
      "modalities": {},
      "nodeId": "9d864136-50a5-4642-9efb-221b5bb422ae",
      "type": "generative_journey"
    },
